      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T17:31:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Henri for the suggestion, agreed it reads better. I applied the syntax change to avctp.pdl, but regenerating avctp.py with the in-tree pdlc (v0.3.3, from out/soong/.../pdlc) produced two issues I wanted to flag.\n\nFirst, the bit shifts on the parent AvctpPacket come out LSB-first even though the file declares big_endian_packets. For example transaction_label ends up at byte0 \u0026 0xf instead of byte0 \u003e\u003e 4, which would misparse every AVCTP header.\n\nSecond, AvctpContinuePacket is dropped from the try-chain in AvctpPacket.parse. Only AvctpSinglePacket and AvctpStartPacket are tried; CONTINUE and END both fall through to the bare base class.\n\nAre these known limitations of this pdlc version, or should I be running a different one? Happy to land just the .pdl change and keep the existing .py for now if that works.",
      "parentUuid": "a36251c7_a28533b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "f93fb783f044da98b660b53df0f302544ae03bf4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24e21b65_4e301818",
        "filename": "tools/bugreport/packets/avctp.pdl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T08:50:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e First, the bit shifts on the parent AvctpPacket come out LSB-first even though the file declares big_endian_packets. For example transaction_label ends up at byte0 \u0026 0xf instead of byte0 \u003e\u003e 4, which would misparse every AVCTP header.\n\nThe field order is not tied to the byte order.\nBig endian packets fields are still LSB first. There is an open discussion about this here: https://github.com/google/pdl/issues/141\n\n\u003e Second, AvctpContinuePacket is dropped from the try-chain in AvctpPacket.parse. Only AvctpSinglePacket and AvctpStartPacket are tried; CONTINUE and END both fall through to the bare base class.\n\nThis is definitely a bug...\nIf you feel motivated I can suggest a quick fix to the python generator script, otherwise feel free to submit as is and fixup later when the PDL fix lands.",
      "parentUuid": "b7f06d3b_da371fc3",
